                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game was released in February 2020... which means that this game came out before the pandemic started, which means that whoever made this game did so with the option of doing literally anything else. But at least they were right about predicting the following years. In that you start off as a small group and eventually turn into a large riot... you convert people to your cause by defeating them with brute force... your only sense of guidance and direction is whatever your cursor happens to be pointing at... your experience here is shorter than expected and nothing happens after you leave earth.\n\nThose are the parallels I came up on the spot, but I'm sure there is more. Like how halfway through you become mentally ill and bored at the same time.\n\nIt’s actually an enjoyable experience, but this made me question the notion of what a game is… because to me this feels like a tutorial to something on a much bigger scale. And I think the fact I wanted more is saying something, I can envision a 6 hour campaign filled with interesting levels and encounters, perhaps even making it into a rogue-like with RPG elements or something! But anyways, what little here is enjoyable… and for the price of an energy drink, I think it’s okay.",
